{
  "about": "The wire of POST /api/setup/status (Prima.SetupStatus), read by apps/cyfr/test/emissary/web/controllers/setup_status_controller_test.exs and apps/codex/internal/setup/status_test.go. exchanges: what the application answers, driven through the endpoint, and what the command line's client reads in that answer. store is what the installation holds: empty, person (a person setup made, with no sign-in method), set_up (they hold one), restore_pending (a restore's claim is pending) or unreachable (the store cannot answer). token is the bearer: setup (the configured token), other, none, basic (the configured token under another scheme) or unconfigured (the configured token's value on a CYFR that configures none). listener is the listener that tagged the request: loopback, proxy or none. padded_to pads the body with spaces to that many bytes. parser marks a body the endpoint's parsers refuse before any pipeline runs, which carries no answer of the route's. answers: what only the client meets, each status and body with its reading. A reading is open, closed, unavailable, update_required (an application without the route) or refused (any other answer: never a guess).",
  "path": "/api/setup/status",
  "version": 1,
  "max_body_bytes": 1024,
  "request": "{\"version\":1}",
  "exchanges": [
